WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:06.336
Rachel Okafor: Morning Peter. How's it going up in Hartford?

2
00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:11.162
Peter Lang: Morning Rachel. Cold but fine. Busy week, open enrollment stuff.

3
00:00:12.065 --> 00:00:22.915
Rachel Okafor: Yeah, I figured. Let's keep this one tight then. I had two things on my list and you had one you wanted to walk me through.

4
00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:28.341
Peter Lang: Right, the PreSense thing. That's the one that's actually causing us pain right now.

5
00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:32.088
Rachel Okafor: Okay, tell me what you're seeing.

6
00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:48.750
Peter Lang: So when a call comes in and our Genesys flow hands it off between queues, or a rep warm transfers it to somebody else, the second agent gets the pop but there's nothing in it. Just an empty frame.

7
00:00:49.004 --> 00:00:51.117
Rachel Okafor: Blank on the receiving side.

8
00:00:52.598 --> 00:01:02.366
Peter Lang: Completely blank. The first agent sees the ad and the pages the caller was on, that all works. Then it transfers and the next person gets a shell.

9
00:01:02.366 --> 00:01:04.110
Peter Lang: No journey, no source, nothing.

10
00:01:04.568 --> 00:01:09.431
Rachel Okafor: And this is only on the transfers, not on the initial pop?

11
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:19.917
Peter Lang: Only transfers. Direct calls are fine. It started maybe two weeks ago, right around when we moved the Medicare queue split.

12
00:01:20.861 --> 00:01:23.453
Rachel Okafor: How many of these are we talking?

13
00:01:24.082 --> 00:01:31.019
Peter Lang: It's probably a quarter of the transfers in the Medicare queue. P and C queues, less, but it happens there too.

14
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.988
Rachel Okafor: And the agents, are they telling you or just working around it?

15
00:01:38.004 --> 00:01:46.128
Peter Lang: Working around it. They just ask the caller again. Which is the whole thing we bought this to avoid, right?

16
00:01:46.778 --> 00:01:57.735
Rachel Okafor: Yeah. Okay. Can you get me a couple of call IDs from this week? Ones where the transfer happened and the second agent got the empty frame?

17
00:01:58.807 --> 00:02:04.026
Peter Lang: I can pull those this afternoon. I'll send them over with the timestamps.

18
00:02:04.568 --> 00:02:08.547
Rachel Okafor: Perfect. And is it every transfer or only certain paths?

19
00:02:09.848 --> 00:02:16.178
Peter Lang: Seems like any transfer where the call changes queue or agent. I haven't found a pattern beyond that.

20
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:25.108
Rachel Okafor: Okay, I'll take that to the team with your examples and see what they say. I'm not going to guess at it here.

21
00:02:25.531 --> 00:02:34.666
Peter Lang: Appreciate it. It's not blocking calls, it's just making the reps look dumb when they ask a caller something we already know.

22
00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:39.175
Rachel Okafor: Understood. Okay, second thing, QM. Where are you on seats?

23
00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:45.817
Peter Lang: We're at sixty two active. We were supposed to be near a hundred by now.

24
00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.791
Rachel Okafor: What's holding it up?

25
00:02:48.244 --> 00:02:57.140
Peter Lang: Honestly just bandwidth. Our supervisors are the ones who have to review and score, and two of them are out on leave.

26
00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.758
Peter Lang: So the rollout's crawling.

27
00:02:59.475 --> 00:03:07.610
Rachel Okafor: Do you want me to do a short session for the supervisors who are still on, just on the scoring side?

28
00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.160
Rachel Okafor: Not the admin stuff.

29
00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:15.781
Peter Lang: That could help. Let me check calendars and get back to you.

30
00:03:16.142 --> 00:03:18.955
Rachel Okafor: Sure. And on volumes, how's October looking?

31
00:03:19.738 --> 00:03:28.007
Peter Lang: Heavy. We're running about eighteen thousand calls a month across the network, maybe twenty two with the open enrollment push.

32
00:03:28.266 --> 00:03:31.079
Rachel Okafor: That's up from what, sixteen in August?

33
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:38.146
Peter Lang: Yeah, sixteen, seventeen. The Google Ads side is doing its job, the conversions are matching fine.

34
00:03:38.867 --> 00:03:42.867
Rachel Okafor: Good. Anything else on the tracking or the Salesforce side?

35
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.828
Peter Lang: No, that's all steady.

36
00:03:45.328 --> 00:03:52.412
Rachel Okafor: Alright. I'll get the transfer thing moving today and follow up on the supervisor session by Thursday.

37
00:03:52.836 --> 00:03:54.477
Peter Lang: Sounds good. Thanks Rachel.

38
00:03:55.899 --> 00:03:57.558
Rachel Okafor: Thanks Peter. Stay warm.
